# Supplementary trust roots, merged into the bundle by gen_crt_bundle.py.
#
# Mozilla retired the original GlobalSign Root CA (R1), so it is no longer in
# cacert.pem. Google Trust Services still cross-signs GTS Root R1 and R4 with
# it, and TfL and the Rail Data Marketplace both serve that cross-signed chain:
#
#     leaf  ->  WR3 / WE1  ->  GTS Root R1 / R4  (issued by GlobalSign Root CA)
#
# GTS Root R1 and R4 are themselves in the Mozilla bundle, and a browser simply
# stops there. esp_crt_bundle.c does not: its verify callback only ever looks up
# the issuer of the *topmost* certificate the server sent, so it asks for the
# retired GlobalSign root and fails the handshake. Without this file, two of the
# five feeds cannot connect at all.
#
# Source: https://curl.se/ca/cacert-2024-03-11.pem
# Verified at generation time by checking that this key actually signs the
# cross-certificates those hosts serve - see docs/gen_crt_bundle.py.
# Subject: CN=GlobalSign Root CA,OU=Root CA,O=GlobalSign nv-sa,C=BE
# Expires: 2028-01-28 12:00:00+00:00
